# Cache policy for a deployment that is entirely static files plus one function.
#
# The exported data is a snapshot of a pipeline run and does not change until it is re-exported,
# so it can be cached hard. Hashed build assets can be cached forever, because a new build
# produces new filenames. Everything else — the HTML shell — must not be cached, or a reader
# would keep loading a stale page after a deploy.
#
# There is no rule for the chat endpoint, and adding one would do nothing: headers declared in
# this file are not applied to responses from Pages Functions, whatever the route matches. The
# function sets its own `Cache-Control: no-store`, which is the only place that can.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
